ComfyUI-BCNodes — models/z_image/dype/

This directory contains code derived from ComfyUI-DyPE
(https://github.com/wildminder/ComfyUI-DyPE), by wildminder and the ComfyUI-DyPE contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory). The sources are the
files src/models/zimage.py (PosEmbedZImage) and src/base.py (the dynamic PI branch of
DyPEBasePosEmbed) at commit 266405844738da9f16e8a072482320168a17c494 (2026-10-24, version 2.20.0).

ComfyUI-DyPE implements DyPE, Dynamic Position Extrapolation, by Noam Issachar, Guy Yariv and
co-authors (https://github.com/guyyariv/DyPE).

Changes made in ComfyUI-BCNodes (embedder.py, with the parts every model shares in
libs/dype/embed.py):
- Every frequency table is computed in float64 on a device that supports it (the CPU otherwise)
  and the rotations are returned in float32, as ComfyUI core's rope; the original computed them in
  bfloat16 on CUDA and float32 elsewhere.
- The method `pi` scales the image positions by scale ** k_t (DY-PI, the original's base-class
  branch). The original's Z-Image embedder sent `pi` to its NTK branch.
- The coordinate resize (_resize_rope_grid) is left out: ComfyUI core's Z-Image image positions
  step by 1 on both image axes, where it returns the positions unchanged. Z-Image Omni's SigLIP
  tokens step by about 8; the original would draw those toward steps of 1 over the run, this port
  leaves them as core places them.
- The shift override of the original installer (src/patch_utils.py, a model_sampling replaced by a
  resolution-dependent ModelSamplingFlux) is not ported: the model's own shift is kept.
- The embedder is built for one sampling step, with that step's scale, timestep and settings
  fixed, and set on the model only for the duration of the step (models/common/dype.py); the
  original set state on one embedder installed as an object patch.
- The image scale is read from the latent of each sampling step (its longer side in pixels over
  base_resolution) in place of the width and height widgets of the original node.
